1
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:21,560
You have to... you have to...

2
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,240
You need to adjust the sound system and mics on site.

3
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:24,639
You can't have the chief speaking...

4
00:02:24,719 --> 00:02:26,000
...and no sound comes out.

5
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:26,960
Did... did something go wrong?

6
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,759
It's unacceptable if the chief goes up and there's no sound.

7
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:29,879
Xiao Qu!

8
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:31,319
Director Tan.

9
00:02:32,159 --> 00:02:32,680
Xiao Qu!

10
00:02:32,919 --> 00:02:33,319
Chief Zhao!

11
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:42,400
Director Tan.

12
00:02:42,639 --> 00:02:43,639
Go on, go on, go on.

13
00:02:43,759 --> 00:02:44,360
Director Tan.

14
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:45,479
Director Yu.

15
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,080
Come here, come here.

16
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:46,599
I have something to discuss with you.

17
00:02:46,599 --> 00:02:47,000
Come, come, come.

18
00:02:52,599 --> 00:02:52,919
Chief Zhao.

19
00:02:53,039 --> 00:02:53,680
Let me see that... that...

20
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:54,400
Chief Guo's... that...

21
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,280
...speech draft.

22
00:03:03,599 --> 00:03:04,960
"Facing what may be a challenging future..."

23
00:03:06,439 --> 00:03:07,080
"And..."

24
00:03:07,719 --> 00:03:08,800
The last sentence is just...

25
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,599
The last issue of the police magazine got a great response.

26
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,919
See if you can expand on Comrade Chen Fei's...

27
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:15,919
...story a bit more.

28
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,000
This is what our Publicity Department should do.

29
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:28,120
You...

30
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,199
Do... do you have a backup?

31
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,039
Get me the backup.

32
00:03:33,439 --> 00:03:34,000
I didn't bring it.

33
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,520
It's on my computer at home.

34
00:03:37,879 --> 00:03:38,919
No... no backup.

35
00:03:38,919 --> 00:03:39,960
This is such a big event, and you...

36
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,159
It's too late for you to go back now.

37
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:41,919
It's starting any minute.

38
00:03:41,919 --> 00:03:42,960
Tell me, what are we going to do?

39
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:43,879
Come on, get up there!

40
00:03:43,879 --> 00:03:44,960
Hurry up and grab it!

41
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,439
Why are you still standing there staring?

42
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,560
Will it come down on its own?

43
00:03:48,439 --> 00:03:49,199
The top of the tree...

44
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:50,639
...can't support my weight, Chief Zhao.

45
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:51,840
What do you mean it can't support...

46
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,039
What did you say in the second half?

47
00:03:53,479 --> 00:03:54,800
"Their spirit will forever illuminate..."

48
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:55,560
"...the path ahead of you."

49
00:03:57,159 --> 00:03:58,000
Can... can you remember...

50
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:58,560
...the rest? The rest of it!

51
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,240
What's wrong, Chief Zhao?

52
00:04:01,639 --> 00:04:02,639
The... the draft I prepared...

53
00:04:02,639 --> 00:04:04,120
The draft I prepared for Chief Guo...

54
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,360
One page was right here...

55
00:04:06,479 --> 00:04:07,479
And it flew... flew up the tree.

56
00:04:08,319 --> 00:04:08,919
It went all the way up there.

57
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:10,439
This... this...

58
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:11,960
Chief Guo!

59
00:04:12,199 --> 00:04:12,840
What was the last sentence?

60
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:13,680
See if you can remember.

61
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,439
Look, look, it's almost time.

62
00:04:16,439 --> 00:04:17,199
What do we do about Chief Guo?

63
00:04:17,439 --> 00:04:18,199
Don't panic, don't panic. Let me see.

64
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:18,959
If you don't get this done...

65
00:04:19,279 --> 00:04:21,439
These young comrades are just so careless in their work!

66
00:04:22,279 --> 00:04:23,160
Who wrote this?

67
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,680
I... I came up with an outline...

68
00:04:26,839 --> 00:04:29,079
And I told Xiao Qu, "You're in charge of..."

69
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,000
"...polishing it up."

70
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,680
And the two pages weren't even stapled together!

71
00:04:32,279 --> 00:04:32,720
Don't panic, don't panic.

72
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,600
Today is such an important event...

73
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,399
What is it, Director Tan?

74
00:04:37,839 --> 00:04:38,920
Are you going to write it yourself?

75
00:04:39,879 --> 00:04:40,720
Just... making a few tweaks.

76
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:43,680
Here, give me the paper.

77
00:04:53,279 --> 00:04:54,040
Did you write this?

78
00:04:58,319 --> 00:04:58,720
Director Tan...

79
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:00,879
I still remember some of the later content.

80
00:05:02,639 --> 00:05:04,199
If a draft flies away, it can be retrieved.

81
00:05:04,839 --> 00:05:06,920
But if an opportunity flies away, it's gone for good.

82
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:14,639
Here,

83
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,560
I also want to lay out

84
00:05:17,399 --> 00:05:19,160
a few expectations for our comrades.

85
00:05:20,319 --> 00:05:20,680
First,

86
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:22,399
continuously strengthen your learning

87
00:05:23,319 --> 00:05:24,360
and improve your own qualities

88
00:05:25,079 --> 00:05:27,399
to adapt to the new demands of public security work in the new era.

89
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:30,560
Second, firmly establish a sense of service.

90
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,759
Always put the interests of the people

91
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:33,839
first.

92
00:05:34,839 --> 00:05:36,160
Put your heart, emotion, and effort

93
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:38,639
into solving the problems that worry,

94
00:05:39,199 --> 00:05:40,720
distress, and trouble the public.

95
00:05:41,399 --> 00:05:43,040
Third, strictly observe discipline

96
00:05:43,639 --> 00:05:44,199
and rules,

97
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:46,279
and build a good image of the police force.

98
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,000
Comrades,

99
00:05:54,759 --> 00:05:55,240
today's Swearing-in Ceremony

100
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:55,600
Director Tan.

101
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:57,399
is not just a look back.

102
00:05:57,519 --> 00:05:58,639
Chief Guo isn't following

103
00:05:58,639 --> 00:05:59,680
the speech you wrote for him.

104
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:00,959
Starting today,

105
00:06:02,199 --> 00:06:02,959
every single one of you

106
00:06:03,399 --> 00:06:04,839
will become a member of the

107
00:06:05,199 --> 00:06:06,519
Red Leaf public security system.

108
00:06:07,199 --> 00:06:07,879
Keep striving.

109
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:12,000
Today's induction

110
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,120
went very smoothly.

111
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:13,439
Yes.

112
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:14,199
It was well organized.

113
00:06:14,199 --> 00:06:14,680
Alright.

114
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,000
Good.

115
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:15,199
Okay.

116
00:06:19,519 --> 00:06:20,839
Chief Guo, this photo looks good.

117
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:22,399
Not bad.

118
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,360
How much were you fined last night?

119
00:06:25,759 --> 00:06:26,439
I wasn't fined.

120
00:06:28,199 --> 00:06:29,439
Who said you could fish here?

121
00:06:29,759 --> 00:06:30,600
I'm talking to you two.

122
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,360
No fishing allowed here.

123
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,879
No one said we couldn't fish.

124
00:06:34,959 --> 00:06:36,519
Can't you see these huge words?

125
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,079
Stop shining that in my eyes.

126
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:39,439
Where's the sign? Where?

127
00:06:39,439 --> 00:06:39,959
I didn't see one.

128
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:40,519
Look here.

129
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,000
No Fishing.

130
00:06:42,279 --> 00:06:43,360
Violators Will Be Heavily Fined.

131
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:45,399
Your sign is in the grass. Who could see it?

132
00:06:45,519 --> 00:06:47,000
I could write "Welcome to Fish" too.

133
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,000
Wipe that smirk off your face.

134
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,199
Xiao Liu, confiscate their gear.

135
00:06:50,199 --> 00:06:51,160
Confiscate what gear?

136
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,040
Let's see who dares to touch it.

137
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,199
You people have no manners.

138
00:06:53,199 --> 00:06:54,000
Fishing here at night,

139
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,160
and getting violent!

140
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:56,439
No one got violent.

141
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:57,439
That's what you say.

142
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,560
I didn't lay a hand on anyone.

143
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:58,920
I'm calling the police.

144
00:06:59,160 --> 00:06:59,360
Call them.

145
00:06:59,560 --> 00:06:59,720
Do it.

146
00:07:00,759 --> 00:07:01,240
Let him call them.

147
00:07:02,319 --> 00:07:02,600
Go ahead and call.

148
00:07:04,319 --> 00:07:04,519
Call them.

149
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:05,439
Call the police.

150
00:07:05,839 --> 00:07:06,519
Call them, call them, call them.

151
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:08,000
Go ahead and call. Come on.

152
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:08,279
You guys,

153
00:07:08,279 --> 00:07:09,199
why call the cops over such a small thing?

154
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:10,480
How much? How much?

155
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,079
Gear confiscated, 300 fine.

156
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:14,279
Don't give him any money!

157
00:07:14,399 --> 00:07:15,959
Absolutely not! Why pay him?

158
00:07:16,399 --> 00:07:16,879
I'll give you 500.

159
00:07:18,879 --> 00:07:20,000
Didn't you write it in the speech?

160
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:20,800
Through thick and thin.

161
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:22,040
I'll pay half.

162
00:07:22,079 --> 00:07:22,959
I really wasn't fined.

163
00:07:23,279 --> 00:07:23,959
With the sign on the ground,

164
00:07:23,959 --> 00:07:24,639
who could see it?

165
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,920
I taught them a lesson.

166
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:30,959
Tan Yan.

167
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:32,759
When it comes to fishing,

168
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:34,759
First, you can't be impatient.

169
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,600
Second, you have to let the line

170
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,519
out a bit longer.

171
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:42,399
Understood.

172
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:54,959
Play the long game.

173
00:09:47,759 --> 00:09:48,720
You know that...

174
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:51,240
Director Yu from the Political Department, right?

175
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:54,399
I think his mom lives in your precinct.

176
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:55,759
You should...

177
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:57,679
...visit her more often.

178
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:59,360
Get to the point.

179
00:09:59,799 --> 00:10:01,720
The director position in our Publicity Department...

180
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,600
...has been vacant for a long time.

181
00:10:03,679 --> 00:10:05,440
There hasn't been any news about it.

182
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,519
I'm skipping breakfast.

183
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:10,240
It's not even 7:30 yet, is it?

184
00:10:11,919 --> 00:10:12,799
There's a case at the station.

185
00:10:13,519 --> 00:10:14,120
I need to go check on it.

186
00:10:14,519 --> 00:10:16,159
Make an effort with Director Yu's mom.

187
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,519
He has a say in my promotion to director.

188
00:10:17,519 --> 00:10:18,159
I'm heading out.

189
00:10:18,559 --> 00:10:19,960
Take some oranges for Vitamin C.

190
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:26,639
Yesterday,

191
00:10:26,919 --> 00:10:29,360
the City Public Security Bureau held a solemn

192
00:10:29,639 --> 00:10:32,440
and grand Swearing-in Ceremony for new officers.

193
00:10:33,039 --> 00:10:34,840
Members of the City Bureau's Party Committee,

194
00:10:35,279 --> 00:10:37,200
representatives of promoted officers,

195
00:10:37,679 --> 00:10:39,879
and heads of various departments

196
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:42,840
witnessed this glorious moment together.

197
00:10:50,039 --> 00:10:51,200
Stealing is stealing.

198
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,240
He was caught red-handed.

199
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:53,240
What else is there to ask?

200
00:10:53,679 --> 00:10:55,159
He's not even 16 yet.

201
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:57,360
Then contact his guardian as soon as possible.

202
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,399
Let me know when his parents arrive.

203
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,759
Why are you acting like this?

204
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:00,639
Acting like what?

205
00:11:00,759 --> 00:11:01,480
Ma'am, ma'am.

206
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:03,000
Please don't panic, okay? Calm down.

207
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:05,000
What's wrong? What happened?

208
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,919
I left my keys inside.

209
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:07,919
The door won't open.

210
00:11:07,919 --> 00:11:09,320
She says she left soup simmering on the stove.

211
00:11:10,159 --> 00:11:11,120
When it comes to unlocking doors,

212
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,039
we police can't really help.

213
00:11:12,039 --> 00:11:13,480
Then what should I do?

214
00:11:14,879 --> 00:11:16,320
Never mind. Help her make a call.

215
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:16,639
You got it.

216
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:17,639
Call a locksmith.

217
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:18,240
Okay.

218
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:18,679
Don't worry.

219
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:19,919
Chief Ji,

220
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,039
this is next week's

221
00:11:21,039 --> 00:11:21,919
plan with Qingshui Community

222
00:11:21,919 --> 00:11:23,120
for the anti-fraud awareness campaign.

223
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:23,799
Take a look.

224
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:26,559
Keep the process as simple as possible.

225
00:11:26,799 --> 00:11:28,120
And make the font on the materials larger.

226
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:28,320
Understood.

227
00:11:28,639 --> 00:11:29,960
The anti-fraud campaign targets

228
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,799
mostly seniors in the community.

229
00:11:31,799 --> 00:11:32,120
Okay.

230
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:32,879
If the font is too small,

231
00:11:32,879 --> 00:11:33,559
they won't be able to read it.

232
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,279
Right, right, right.

233
00:11:38,159 --> 00:11:38,960
What's going on here?

234
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,200
That guy had too much to drink.

235
00:11:42,279 --> 00:11:43,240
Officer Li brought him in from patrol.

236
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:44,679
You need to wake him up.

237
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:45,919
This is a police station,

238
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:46,759
not a hotel.

239
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:48,159
Hurry up and get him out of here.

240
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:48,519
I...

241
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:49,600
Okay.

242
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:54,360
Chief Ji.

243
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:55,960
Xiaomin.

244
00:11:56,919 --> 00:11:57,320
Xiaomin!

245
00:11:57,840 --> 00:11:58,960
Mr. Jin, Mr. Jin!

246
00:11:59,360 --> 00:11:59,960
What's wrong?

247
00:12:00,519 --> 00:12:01,039
Xiaomin...

248
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:05,919
Gangzi is missing again.

249
00:12:05,919 --> 00:12:07,559
Did... did you call him?

250
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:08,960
I did. Look.

251
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:11,440
Where are my glasses?

252
00:12:11,519 --> 00:12:11,720
I...

253
00:12:11,799 --> 00:12:12,240
On your head.

254
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:12,600
Right here.

255
00:12:13,679 --> 00:12:14,039
Look.

256
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:14,879
Don't panic.

257
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:15,799
I'll call him.

258
00:12:16,039 --> 00:12:16,840
Just don't panic.

259
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:17,840
Let's go, let's go.

260
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:18,480
Hurry up, hurry up!

261
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:34,519
Morning, Director Tan.

262
00:12:34,799 --> 00:12:35,240
Morning.

263
00:12:36,879 --> 00:12:38,240
How come you're reading "The Art of War"?

264
00:12:38,519 --> 00:12:39,320
Chief Zhao recommended it.

265
00:12:39,559 --> 00:12:41,080
He said I could learn about

266
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:42,279
The Art of Illusion and Reality.

267
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:43,799
When to draw your sword,

268
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,120
and when to conceal your blade.

269
00:12:45,399 --> 00:12:46,639
That's true mastery.

270
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:58,679
Where's Chief Zhao?

271
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:00,799
He took a call from Director Yu and stepped out.

272
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:03,159
What was it about?

273
00:13:04,919 --> 00:13:05,480
Not sure.

274
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:08,360
All I heard was Chief Zhao repeatedly saying,

275
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:08,879
"You're welcome."

276
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,320
Come in, Chief Zhao.

277
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:21,759
Please.

278
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,519
I'm telling you, Chief Zhao,

279
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,240
you really solved a huge problem for me.

280
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,399
Not at all, it was nothing.

281
00:13:27,519 --> 00:13:27,919
Some other time,

282
00:13:27,919 --> 00:13:29,360
I'll definitely treat you to a meal.

283
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,639
No, Director, I should treat you.

284
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:32,360
You have no idea

285
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:33,960
how much this was stressing me out.

286
00:13:34,639 --> 00:13:35,759
Every day, my wife...

287
00:13:38,519 --> 00:13:38,759
Director.

288
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:40,519
All right then, Director.

289
00:13:40,519 --> 00:13:41,480
I'll... I'll get going now.

290
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,159
All right, all right.

291
00:13:42,159 --> 00:13:42,759
Chief Zhao,

292
00:13:42,759 --> 00:13:43,240
some other day!

293
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:44,039
We must have that meal!

294
00:13:44,039 --> 00:13:44,799
Don't worry, we will.

295
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:45,399
Okay.

296
00:13:47,639 --> 00:13:48,759
Director, is this a good time?

297
00:13:49,639 --> 00:13:50,039
It is.

298
00:13:51,519 --> 00:13:52,279
Let me take this call.

299
00:13:53,639 --> 00:13:54,840
Excuse me, I need to take this.

300
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:56,039
Go ahead.

301
00:13:57,279 --> 00:13:59,080
Right, right. Okay, okay.

302
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:20,000
Anyway, if there are any updates on your end,

303
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,440
just let me know as soon as possible.

304
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,879
It'll help us advance our publicity work.

305
00:14:24,919 --> 00:14:26,200
I won't pry into the details of the case.

306
00:14:28,879 --> 00:14:30,159
It's all for the sake of the job.

307
00:14:30,279 --> 00:14:31,279
We're all just doing our jobs.

308
00:14:32,919 --> 00:14:33,240
Okay.

309
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:34,960
Okay.

310
00:14:45,159 --> 00:14:47,440
Chief Zhao, about the new recruits' art event...

311
00:14:47,879 --> 00:14:48,759
Could you take a look?

312
00:14:49,399 --> 00:14:49,919
No need.

313
00:14:50,559 --> 00:14:51,799
You're the lead deputy director.

314
00:14:51,799 --> 00:14:52,679
As long as you've reviewed it, it's fine.

315
00:14:53,399 --> 00:14:54,799
Then I'll arrange it as I see fit.

316
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:56,240
Director Tan.

317
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:58,720
You're the professional in publicity.

318
00:14:58,919 --> 00:15:00,399
I just switched to this field halfway.

319
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:02,320
I still have to ask for your advice on many things.

320
00:15:03,039 --> 00:15:04,159
Chief Zhao, you flatter me.

321
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,559
We still need to learn from each other.

322
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:07,919
Share resources.

323
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,240
Through thick and thin.

324
00:15:10,559 --> 00:15:11,279
Through thick and thin.

325
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:15,559
We must follow up promptly on any operations.

326
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,080
To get first-hand material.

327
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,000
You're absolutely right.

328
00:15:22,639 --> 00:15:23,960
I'm accompanying Chief Guo for an interview.

329
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:25,919
Do you need me to go?

330
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:27,799
I'll go with you.

331
00:15:27,919 --> 00:15:28,720
No, no, no need.

332
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:31,200
Chief Zhao.

333
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:32,759
Director Tan.

334
00:15:33,159 --> 00:15:34,679
The materials you requested on Comrade Chen Fei

335
00:15:34,679 --> 00:15:35,919
and his heroic injury have been compiled.

336
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:37,799
It's just that...

337
00:15:38,879 --> 00:15:40,480
Comrade Chen Fei's last words before his coma...

338
00:15:40,679 --> 00:15:41,159
Can't be included.

339
00:15:42,799 --> 00:15:43,200
Why not?

340
00:15:43,679 --> 00:15:44,559
It's profanity.

341
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:45,720
What did he say?

342
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:46,759
He said...

343
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,120
"Screw your grandma."

344
00:15:50,639 --> 00:15:51,720
Yeah, we definitely can't write that.

345
00:15:54,679 --> 00:15:56,519
Are there any vice sweeps today?

346
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,320
I haven't heard of any operations.

347
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:00,879
Chief Zhao never mentioned it.

348
00:16:24,519 --> 00:16:27,720
Sorry, the number you dialed is temporarily...

349
00:16:35,679 --> 00:16:38,000
Sorry, the number you dialed...

350
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,200
Hung up on me.

351
00:16:48,679 --> 00:16:49,840
I'm working. Are you crazy?

352
00:16:51,039 --> 00:16:51,639
I'm crazy?

353
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:52,720
Where are you working?

354
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:53,679
Give me your location.

355
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,319
What's wrong with the network?

356
00:17:13,319 --> 00:17:14,400
Can someone go check it?

357
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:15,319
Hurry up.

358
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,359
The rat's still in the hole.

359
00:17:31,599 --> 00:17:32,359
Keep a close eye on the outside.

360
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,279
Report back every ten minutes.

361
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:34,920
Copy that.

362
00:17:49,519 --> 00:17:49,920
Captain Zhang.

363
00:17:50,599 --> 00:17:51,759
I've got a suspicious person here.

364
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:53,000
At three o'clock.

365
00:17:53,279 --> 00:17:53,839
Wearing a mask.

366
00:17:58,759 --> 00:17:59,359
Ignore him.

367
00:17:59,359 --> 00:18:00,119
He's a colleague.

368
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:08,880
Wait, you actually came?

369
00:18:28,799 --> 00:18:30,000
Why cover yourself up so much?

370
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,400
Are you crazy?

371
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,799
Professionalism. Don't you know?

372
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,799
Can't let the suspects

373
00:18:38,799 --> 00:18:39,720
remember my face.

374
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:40,359
Alright, alright.

375
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,480
Get me a bulletproof vest.

376
00:18:45,279 --> 00:18:45,640
Don't have one.

377
00:18:47,599 --> 00:18:48,400
Take yours off for me.

378
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:49,359
I'm not wearing one.

379
00:18:51,559 --> 00:18:52,799
What are you doing? I'm really not.

380
00:18:55,079 --> 00:18:56,480
Looks like your operation this time

381
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,720
isn't that dangerous.

382
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:01,680
I thought it was super dangerous

383
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:02,519
with such a big setup.

384
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:06,200
How many days have you been staking out?

385
00:19:07,839 --> 00:19:08,440
Seven days.

386
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:11,960
That's not easy.

387
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:17,720
Can you cut the nonsense?

388
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:18,839
Time is precious.

389
00:19:19,359 --> 00:19:21,000
You do your job, I'll do mine.

390
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:22,519
Do you know what I'm here for?

391
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:29,920
Nothing worth publicizing.

392
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,400
That girl in the tank top,

393
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:37,759
what's her deal? What did she do?

394
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:39,240
Selling Rock sugar.

395
00:19:40,759 --> 00:19:41,559
A new type of drug?

396
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:44,599
I suspect

397
00:19:44,599 --> 00:19:46,640
it's the one the whole bureau was briefed on,

398
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:47,880
the new drug Spring Snow,

399
00:19:50,279 --> 00:19:51,160
appearing in Red Leaf.

400
00:19:53,359 --> 00:19:53,920
I'm not sure,

401
00:19:54,759 --> 00:19:55,880
but the price matches.

402
00:19:57,799 --> 00:19:59,319
If you follow the trail

403
00:19:59,559 --> 00:20:00,839
and catch her supplier,

404
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,039
that's another achievement.

405
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:09,359
Jealous?

406
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:10,680
I'm jealous.

407
00:20:12,599 --> 00:20:13,839
I'll give you a chance to contribute.

408
00:20:13,839 --> 00:20:14,400
Do you want it?

409
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:15,240
What is it?

410
00:20:17,359 --> 00:20:18,599
The guys haven't eaten yet.

411
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:20,160
Help us sort that out.

412
00:20:20,599 --> 00:20:22,000
I'm a deputy director of the Publicity Department...

413
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:23,200
Then forget it.

414
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:27,279
Sichuan, Hunan, or hot pot?

415
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:31,039
Hot pot. Nine-grid.

416
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:35,279
We really need the smell of that nine-grid

417
00:20:35,279 --> 00:20:37,359
to cover up your body odor.

418
00:20:38,279 --> 00:20:39,240
Smell it, smell.

419
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:18,079
Baobao.

420
00:21:55,039 --> 00:21:55,759
Dress right!

421
00:21:58,119 --> 00:21:58,640
Eyes front!

422
00:21:59,279 --> 00:21:59,559
Attention!

423
00:22:00,480 --> 00:22:01,480
During the patrol later,

424
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:03,319
mind your bearing and discipline, and be polite.

425
00:22:03,799 --> 00:22:04,680
To the left and right, face!

426
00:22:06,079 --> 00:22:06,640
Begin patrol!

427
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:40,119
Pengpeng.

428
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:41,720
Here's your water.

429
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:42,400
This is useless.

430
00:22:46,759 --> 00:22:47,480
I want a Coke.

431
00:22:49,480 --> 00:22:50,319
Too much sugar.

432
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:51,759
It'll make you sleepy.

433
00:23:03,839 --> 00:23:04,440
Good for nothing.

434
00:23:17,599 --> 00:23:18,799
Rock sugar is heading out. Move out.

435
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:20,200
Let's go.

436
00:24:00,559 --> 00:24:02,240
Captain Zhang, Rock sugar has stopped.

437
00:24:02,559 --> 00:24:03,200
She entered the night market street.

438
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:04,160
Follow her.

439
00:24:04,799 --> 00:24:05,839
Be careful. Don't spook them.

440
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:08,640
Turn sideways, Pengpeng. Pengpeng!

441
00:24:10,599 --> 00:24:10,920
Looking good.

442
00:24:11,039 --> 00:24:13,079
Can you give it a rest, Old Tan?

443
00:24:13,079 --> 00:24:14,279
So cool. So cool.

444
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:20,039
Crimson Tassel Binds the Drug Demon.

445
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:22,319
Red Leaf Police Show Their Bravery.

446
00:24:22,559 --> 00:24:23,640
What do you think of this title?

447
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:24,640
Over the top.

448
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:25,960
You don't understand.

449
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:29,359
We're in the age of new media now.

450
00:24:29,599 --> 00:24:30,920
The theme needs to stand out

451
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:32,880
so people know what you're doing.

452
00:24:34,319 --> 00:24:35,359
Pengpeng. Pengpeng.

453
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:36,720
Give me one more. Come on.

454
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,000
Turn a bit. Turn a bit, Pengpeng.

455
00:24:38,839 --> 00:24:40,440
Let me give you a riddle, alright?

456
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:43,680
Twenty-six letters.

457
00:24:44,319 --> 00:24:44,839
ET left.

458
00:24:45,759 --> 00:24:46,319
How many are left?

459
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:47,599
Who left?

460
00:24:48,039 --> 00:24:48,400
ET.

461
00:24:48,839 --> 00:24:49,519
E and T.

462
00:24:49,559 --> 00:24:50,720
Tell you what, if you guess right,

463
00:24:51,119 --> 00:24:52,720
I'll pay for our reunion dinner, okay?

464
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:43,559
Has the buyer shown up?

465
00:25:44,359 --> 00:25:44,839
Not yet.

466
00:25:45,359 --> 00:25:47,440
This girl is chatting with every vendor she sees.

467
00:25:47,599 --> 00:25:49,000
She really looks like she's just here to shop.

468
00:25:49,599 --> 00:25:50,599
Don't let your guard down.

469
00:25:50,599 --> 00:25:51,920
The buyer might be right around them.

470
00:25:52,359 --> 00:25:52,599
Keep a close watch.

471
00:25:52,599 --> 00:25:53,480
ET left.

472
00:25:54,480 --> 00:25:56,200
A, B, C, D, E, F, G...

473
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:06,920
Excuse me, let me take another look at this bag.

474
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:13,759
How much is this bag?

475
00:26:14,160 --> 00:26:14,559
Forty.

476
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:21,880
Can you make it cheaper?

477
00:26:23,640 --> 00:26:24,400
Just keep looking, then.

478
00:26:24,599 --> 00:26:25,160
Okay, thanks.

479
00:26:25,519 --> 00:26:27,039
Captain Zhang, the target left.

480
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:28,799
Wait.

481
00:26:29,599 --> 00:26:30,519
Looks like she took the wrong bag.

482
00:26:31,160 --> 00:26:31,640
Where's her bag?

483
00:26:34,039 --> 00:26:34,960
The customer next to her took it.

484
00:26:35,119 --> 00:26:36,480
Move in! The one with the bag is the buyer.

485
00:26:38,359 --> 00:26:38,799
Police!

486
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:39,279
Don't move!

487
00:26:39,279 --> 00:26:39,640
Freeze!

488
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:47,240
Stop! Don't run!

489
00:26:51,559 --> 00:26:52,119
Stop!

490
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:53,000
Stop!

491
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:53,480
Don't run!

492
00:27:09,799 --> 00:27:10,559
You okay? Are you hurt?

493
00:27:15,680 --> 00:27:16,240
Freeze!

494
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:17,440
Move! Get out of the way!

495
00:27:22,319 --> 00:27:22,799
Move aside!

496
00:27:24,759 --> 00:27:25,240
Stop it!

497
00:27:26,839 --> 00:27:27,279
Don't move!

498
00:27:27,279 --> 00:27:27,799
Let go!

499
00:27:29,559 --> 00:27:30,119
They have guns!

500
00:27:30,599 --> 00:27:31,079
Stop!

501
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:33,920
We are the police!

502
00:27:34,519 --> 00:27:34,960
Don't shoot!

503
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:35,680
Police! Police!

504
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:36,440
We're the police!

505
00:27:36,440 --> 00:27:36,759
Narcotics!

506
00:27:36,759 --> 00:27:37,599
We're on a mission!

507
00:27:38,160 --> 00:27:38,680
Are you okay?

508
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,200
Come in. Come in. What's your status?

509
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:52,079
Captain Zhang, we got grabbed by the Special Police!

510
00:28:00,559 --> 00:28:01,279
Watch your tone!

511
00:28:01,279 --> 00:28:01,799
What are you doing?

512
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:03,039
Captain Zhang!

513
00:28:03,440 --> 00:28:04,880
They pointed their guns at our heads!

514
00:28:05,039 --> 00:28:05,759
That's why the suspect got away!

515
00:28:05,759 --> 00:28:06,519
If it weren't for them,

516
00:28:06,519 --> 00:28:07,480
we would have caught him already!

517
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:07,680
Yeah!

518
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:09,559
You guys in the Special Police are really something!

519
00:28:10,359 --> 00:28:11,599
If this suspect gets away,

520
00:28:11,839 --> 00:28:13,559
can you Special Police take responsibility for it?

521
00:28:15,839 --> 00:28:17,039
Take what responsibility?

522
00:28:17,759 --> 00:28:18,079
Chief Liao.

523
00:28:18,400 --> 00:28:18,759
Chief Liao.

524
00:28:25,960 --> 00:28:26,359
Captain Zhang.

525
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:27,079
Chief Liao.

526
00:28:27,519 --> 00:28:29,119
Is it written on your men's faces?

527
00:28:29,119 --> 00:28:30,039
How were we supposed to know?

528
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:32,599
What do you mean, written on their faces?

529
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:34,039
What's with your attitude?

530
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:35,039
What's wrong with my attitude?

531
00:28:35,039 --> 00:28:36,000
What's with your attitude?

532
00:28:36,119 --> 00:28:36,920
What's with your attitude?!

533
00:28:36,920 --> 00:28:38,440
I'm working a case today.

534
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:38,920
I need to make an arrest.

535
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:39,880
You tell me, what's with your attitude?

536
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:41,319
Here, look at this.

537
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,559
If you want him, follow protocol.

538
00:28:43,880 --> 00:28:44,640
Gentlemen! Gentlemen!

539
00:28:45,039 --> 00:28:46,039
I'm from the City...

540
00:28:46,400 --> 00:28:47,839
Tan Yan, from the City Bureau's Publicity Department.

541
00:28:49,039 --> 00:28:50,839
I'd like to interview both of you captains.

542
00:28:56,079 --> 00:28:56,519
Captain Zhang,

543
00:28:57,359 --> 00:28:59,279
please tell us about your joint operation

544
00:28:59,279 --> 00:28:59,839
with the Special Police Unit this time.

545
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:01,480
What would you like to say?

546
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:05,200
Your lens cap.

547
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:17,480
Thank you.

548
00:29:19,039 --> 00:29:20,359
Thanks to the officers of the Special Police Unit

549
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:24,960
for helping us

550
00:29:25,079 --> 00:29:26,200
complete this mission together.

551
00:29:28,279 --> 00:29:28,640
Chief Liao.

552
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:29,839
Got it.

553
00:29:30,279 --> 00:29:31,880
The Special Police Unit's actions in this operation

554
00:29:32,200 --> 00:29:34,119
were perfectly timed and highly effective.

555
00:29:34,759 --> 00:29:35,359
What are you trying to say?

556
00:29:43,759 --> 00:29:44,400
Then take him.

557
00:29:52,519 --> 00:29:53,440
You owe me a meal.

558
00:29:55,839 --> 00:29:56,680
Alright, I owe you a meal.

559
00:29:57,319 --> 00:29:58,160
I owe you a meal.

560
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:00,279
For this mission,

561
00:30:00,519 --> 00:30:01,359
to all our police officers,

562
00:30:01,880 --> 00:30:02,680
thank you for your hard work.

563
00:30:03,200 --> 00:30:03,640
A round of applause.

564
00:30:04,599 --> 00:30:04,839
Good.

565
00:30:05,119 --> 00:30:05,920
Thank you for your hard work, officers.

566
00:30:16,119 --> 00:30:16,920
Morning, Director Tan.

567
00:30:21,759 --> 00:30:23,000
Is this how police officers act?

568
00:30:23,559 --> 00:30:24,400
Fighting over a suspect on the street.

569
00:30:25,680 --> 00:30:26,240
Do you all want to go

570
00:30:26,240 --> 00:30:27,599
report to Internal Affairs?

571
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:36,799
Chief Guo,

572
00:30:37,640 --> 00:30:40,440
we do bear responsibility for this.

573
00:30:41,079 --> 00:30:41,920
What responsibility?

574
00:30:44,839 --> 00:30:45,440
Chief Guo,

575
00:30:46,759 --> 00:30:48,359
we helped them catch the guy,

576
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:50,880
but instead of thanking us, Captain Zhang

577
00:30:51,839 --> 00:30:53,200
immediately wants us to take the blame.

578
00:30:54,279 --> 00:30:54,799
That's unacceptable.

579
00:30:54,799 --> 00:30:55,200
Wait a minute.

580
00:30:55,200 --> 00:30:56,880
What do you mean, you helped us catch the guy?

581
00:30:57,440 --> 00:30:58,400
If you hadn't interfered,

582
00:30:58,400 --> 00:30:59,759
we would've caught the suspect long ago.

583
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:00,920
And I'd also like to ask,

584
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:02,279
if he had gotten away,

585
00:31:02,720 --> 00:31:04,160
could the Special Police Unit take the blame?

586
00:31:04,160 --> 00:31:05,079
Did he get away?

587
00:31:06,519 --> 00:31:07,440
I said "if."

588
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:08,920
I'm not here to debate the outcome with you.

589
00:31:08,920 --> 00:31:09,759
Enough!

590
00:31:21,839 --> 00:31:22,240
Chief Guo.

591
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:23,480
Let me state my position.

592
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:27,480
Technically, this is

593
00:31:28,079 --> 00:31:29,720
a case the Narcotics Squad has been on for a long time.

594
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:32,839
Even though the suspect was ultimately

595
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:33,640
caught by the Special Police Unit,

596
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:34,640
no matter how you look at it,

597
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:37,079
the suspect should be handed over to Captain Zhang.

598
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:38,440
This time,

599
00:31:38,440 --> 00:31:40,319
it's mainly because our two units didn't

600
00:31:40,319 --> 00:31:41,000
coordinate in advance.

601
00:31:41,440 --> 00:31:41,839
Of course,

602
00:31:42,119 --> 00:31:43,920
we definitely didn't handle things properly.

603
00:31:44,359 --> 00:31:44,880
For this,

604
00:31:44,880 --> 00:31:46,640
as the political commissar, I take responsibility.

605
00:31:47,119 --> 00:31:48,559
I'll go back and write a

606
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:51,440
thorough and detailed self-criticism report.

607
00:31:53,079 --> 00:31:54,799
Captain Zhang, I apologize.

608
00:32:06,039 --> 00:32:06,400
Come in.

609
00:32:08,279 --> 00:32:09,119
Chief Guo, you wanted to see me?

610
00:32:09,119 --> 00:32:09,880
Tan Yan, come over here.

611
00:32:15,200 --> 00:32:17,440
You were at the scene last night.

612
00:32:17,599 --> 00:32:17,920
I was.

613
00:32:18,119 --> 00:32:19,119
Give us an objective account

614
00:32:19,440 --> 00:32:20,039
of what happened.

615
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:22,880
Objectively speaking,

616
00:32:22,960 --> 00:32:23,880
it was a misunderstanding.

617
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:25,480
Just a clash of circumstances.

618
00:32:26,440 --> 00:32:27,599
The Special Police Unit on patrol

619
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:29,359
naturally puts the public's safety

620
00:32:29,359 --> 00:32:30,039
as their top priority.

621
00:32:30,599 --> 00:32:31,599
Seeing three grown men

622
00:32:31,599 --> 00:32:32,519
chasing a little girl,

623
00:32:33,119 --> 00:32:34,680
it's understandable they rushed in.

624
00:32:35,519 --> 00:32:37,359
As for the Narcotics Squad, they staked out for days.

625
00:32:38,079 --> 00:32:38,440
How many days?

626
00:32:40,039 --> 00:32:40,559
Seven days.

627
00:32:41,680 --> 00:32:42,039
Seven days.

628
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:44,359
Right before making the bust,

629
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:46,400
they were tackled by the Special Police Unit.

630
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:47,279
Put yourself in their shoes.

631
00:32:47,440 --> 00:32:48,400
If this happened to anyone,

632
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:49,720
who wouldn't be furious?

633
00:32:49,720 --> 00:32:50,759
Getting into an argument on the street

634
00:32:51,519 --> 00:32:52,480
is also understandable.

635
00:32:54,400 --> 00:32:55,200
Wow, Tan Yan.

636
00:32:56,119 --> 00:32:57,359
You have a real way with words.

637
00:32:57,720 --> 00:32:58,559
You didn't offend anyone.

638
00:33:00,359 --> 00:33:01,039
Chief Guo, I...

639
00:33:02,400 --> 00:33:04,000
I'm just objectively discussing the facts.

640
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:05,920
That's well said.

641
00:33:06,920 --> 00:33:09,599
Objectively discussing the facts.

642
00:33:10,519 --> 00:33:11,720
Whatever we do,

643
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:13,799
we can't just consider our own perspective.

644
00:33:15,079 --> 00:33:16,480
Cops on the street,

645
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:17,880
two units arguing with each other.

646
00:33:17,880 --> 00:33:18,920
While civilians watch the show.

647
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:20,880
Where is the police image?

648
00:33:22,359 --> 00:33:23,200
Where is our enforcement authority?

649
00:33:23,680 --> 00:33:24,400
Our collective honor...

650
00:33:25,640 --> 00:33:26,119
where is it?

651
00:33:26,960 --> 00:33:27,759
Where did you leave it all?

652
00:33:30,039 --> 00:33:31,079
Go back and reflect on this.

653
00:33:31,279 --> 00:33:32,920
Let this be a lesson. Don't do it again.

654
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:34,799
Yes, sir.

655
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:37,880
Yes, sir.

656
00:33:38,799 --> 00:33:39,319
Yes, sir.

657
00:33:43,279 --> 00:33:44,599
You handled the situation last night

658
00:33:44,599 --> 00:33:45,319
very well.

659
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:46,640
You managed to salvage

660
00:33:46,640 --> 00:33:48,039
the image of our Red Leaf Police in time.

661
00:33:48,319 --> 00:33:49,160
You deserve to be praised.

662
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:51,519
Chief Guo, I didn't actually do much.

663
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:53,279
It's true that the two Captains

664
00:33:53,279 --> 00:33:54,000
were at their boiling point.

665
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:55,160
But with a little reminder from me,

666
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:56,519
they immediately calmed down.

667
00:33:56,680 --> 00:33:57,160
You see?

668
00:33:57,920 --> 00:33:59,839
Our comrades from the Publicity Department

669
00:34:00,319 --> 00:34:01,880
when handling public opinion,

670
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:04,119
really know how to stay sharp.

671
00:34:04,920 --> 00:34:05,599
Keep it up.

672
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:08,440
Always sharp. I don't dare slack off.

673
00:34:16,239 --> 00:34:17,079
See you later, Captain Zhang.

674
00:34:22,760 --> 00:34:23,559
How many grams did you seize?

675
00:34:26,519 --> 00:34:27,360
All for nothing.

676
00:34:28,480 --> 00:34:30,000
The girl was selling real rock sugar.

677
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:34,559
What about the buyer?

678
00:34:35,639 --> 00:34:36,840
The buyer is just a junkie.

679
00:34:37,880 --> 00:34:39,679
His craving kicked in, completely clueless.

680
00:34:40,400 --> 00:34:41,159
He just got scammed.

681
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:45,480
What a waste of the great headline I came up with.

682
00:34:46,880 --> 00:34:47,320
What headline?

683
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:51,239
Crimson Tassel Binds the Drug Demon.

684
00:34:57,960 --> 00:34:59,960
First he says it's excusable,

685
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:03,199
then he says to put ourselves in their shoes.

686
00:35:06,760 --> 00:35:08,840
Tan Yan is just smoothing things over and taking sides!

687
00:35:10,119 --> 00:35:12,440
Everyone knows how close he is to Zhang Peng.

688
00:35:13,119 --> 00:35:14,599
But Chief Guo buys it completely.

689
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:17,199
There you go again.

690
00:35:18,119 --> 00:35:19,320
With your temper,

691
00:35:19,559 --> 00:35:20,880
if you really clashed with Zhang Peng,

692
00:35:21,159 --> 00:35:23,239
without Director Tan stepping in to mediate,

693
00:35:23,639 --> 00:35:25,000
things would have gotten out of hand.

694
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:26,679
It's not like we did anything wrong.

695
00:35:26,679 --> 00:35:27,400
What are we afraid of?

696
00:35:27,920 --> 00:35:29,159
I don't care how far this escalates.

697
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:29,800
Brother,

698
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:31,840
I'm afraid. Is that okay?

699
00:35:31,840 --> 00:35:32,440
Then what are you afraid of?

700
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:38,599
We have the provincial competition coming up.

701
00:35:39,079 --> 00:35:39,679
But look at us now.

702
00:35:40,360 --> 00:35:42,079
We still don't have a training ground,

703
00:35:42,159 --> 00:35:43,119
and the equipment funding isn't resolved.

704
00:35:44,239 --> 00:35:45,079
The application we submitted

705
00:35:45,480 --> 00:35:46,440
is still held up at the City Bureau.

706
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:47,800
At a crucial time like this,

707
00:35:47,800 --> 00:35:48,960
can we please not cause any trouble?

708
00:35:51,639 --> 00:35:52,320
The competition again.

709
00:35:54,079 --> 00:35:55,000
They want the horse to run,

710
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:57,159
but won't let it graze.

711
00:35:58,079 --> 00:35:59,599
We have nothing. How can we compete?

712
00:36:00,559 --> 00:36:01,039
We just can't.

713
00:36:03,079 --> 00:36:04,559
No, can you not say that?

714
00:36:05,599 --> 00:36:06,000
What?

715
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:08,079
Just because they look down on us,

716
00:36:08,159 --> 00:36:09,360
does that mean we have to

717
00:36:09,360 --> 00:36:10,280
look down on ourselves too?

718
00:36:10,719 --> 00:36:11,960
We step up when we have the means,

719
00:36:11,960 --> 00:36:14,119
and we create the means when we don't.

720
00:36:14,599 --> 00:36:15,519
Just get it done.

721
00:36:20,880 --> 00:36:21,159
Director Tan.

722
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:22,440
Director Tan.

723
00:36:22,440 --> 00:36:23,079
Morning, Director Tan.

724
00:36:33,480 --> 00:36:34,000
Director Tan.

725
00:36:36,079 --> 00:36:36,559
I heard

726
00:36:37,119 --> 00:36:39,679
Narcotics and Special Police clashed on the street last night.

727
00:36:41,079 --> 00:36:41,360
Who said that?

728
00:36:42,280 --> 00:36:43,440
Who said they clashed?

729
00:36:44,199 --> 00:36:45,159
I was right there at the scene.

730
00:36:45,719 --> 00:36:46,639
Don't spread rumors.

731
00:36:46,760 --> 00:36:47,280
Director Tan,

732
00:36:47,679 --> 00:36:48,960
everyone is talking about it.

733
00:36:49,199 --> 00:36:50,239
They said you were the one

734
00:36:50,360 --> 00:36:51,280
who handled public opinion at the scene.

735
00:36:53,400 --> 00:36:55,119
You stopped the situation from escalating,

736
00:36:55,559 --> 00:36:57,599
and explained things to the public in time.

737
00:36:57,840 --> 00:36:59,519
Maintaining the image of the police

738
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:02,360
is exactly our Publicity Department's job.

739
00:37:05,119 --> 00:37:06,719
In that case, Director Tan,

740
00:37:07,360 --> 00:37:08,760
you definitely earned a merit this time.

741
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:14,599
Director Tan is indeed capable.

742
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:16,599
If it were anyone else,

743
00:37:16,599 --> 00:37:17,719
they wouldn't have handled it well.

744
00:37:21,320 --> 00:37:22,559
Chief Zhao, I can't speak for others,

745
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:23,840
but if you were at the scene,

746
00:37:24,360 --> 00:37:26,519
you definitely would've handled it better.

747
00:37:27,119 --> 00:37:28,159
Not me. Not me.

748
00:37:28,320 --> 00:37:28,960
I couldn't handle it.

749
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:30,599
Without a friend in the Narcotics Squad,

750
00:37:30,760 --> 00:37:31,559
I couldn't have gotten involved anyway.

751
00:37:38,239 --> 00:37:39,360
Xiao Qu, let me ask you a question.

752
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,159
How many letters are in the English alphabet?

753
00:37:43,920 --> 00:37:44,719
Twenty-six.

754
00:37:46,079 --> 00:37:47,280
Right, twenty-six.

755
00:37:48,039 --> 00:37:49,320
If E and T left,

756
00:37:49,599 --> 00:37:50,400
how many letters are left?

757
00:37:51,639 --> 00:37:52,239
Twenty-four.

758
00:37:52,679 --> 00:37:53,079
Wrong.

759
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:54,880
Think carefully.

760
00:37:55,559 --> 00:37:56,440
Twenty-six...

761
00:37:56,760 --> 00:37:58,159
Two left, so isn't it twenty-four?

762
00:37:58,559 --> 00:37:59,039
Wrong.

763
00:37:59,719 --> 00:38:01,119
Young man, use your brain.

764
00:38:01,280 --> 00:38:01,719
Think about it.

765
00:38:03,320 --> 00:38:03,880
Do the math.

766
00:38:11,239 --> 00:38:12,480
Where did E and T go?

767
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:18,960
Yeah, where did they go?

768
00:38:19,159 --> 00:38:20,960
They took a UFO to get skewers.

769
00:38:22,039 --> 00:38:22,960
To get skewers?

770
00:38:26,960 --> 00:38:27,639
You guys...

771
00:38:27,920 --> 00:38:30,480
notify me immediately when there's an operation.

772
00:38:31,199 --> 00:38:33,639
Whether I get promoted to chief this time

773
00:38:33,920 --> 00:38:36,920
depends on how well I handle my upcoming tasks.

774
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:53,239
What's up, Lao Tan?

775
00:38:53,880 --> 00:38:55,519
Didn't Chief Guo just praise you?

776
00:38:56,079 --> 00:38:56,559
Yeah.

777
00:38:57,039 --> 00:38:57,840
I heard about it too.

778
00:38:58,320 --> 00:39:00,239
That private office shouldn't be a problem, right?

779
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:02,679
You have no respect for your elders.

780
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:04,119
What's wrong with letting an older comrade have it?

781
00:39:07,840 --> 00:39:09,239
The older comrades...

782
00:39:10,280 --> 00:39:11,760
...are eyeing it like hawks.

783
00:39:11,920 --> 00:39:14,119
This isn't something you just give away.

784
00:39:40,519 --> 00:39:40,840
Boss

785
00:39:54,360 --> 00:39:54,639
Bet blind.

786
00:40:05,639 --> 00:40:06,639
You've got some nerve.

787
00:40:30,440 --> 00:40:31,079
Boss Bai.

788
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:33,480
Let's

789
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:36,559
raise the stakes.

790
00:40:39,199 --> 00:40:39,719
Raise the stakes.

791
00:40:41,519 --> 00:40:42,360
You're out of money.

792
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:43,440
How can you play against me?

793
00:40:49,920 --> 00:40:50,840
Then let's bet our lives.

794
00:41:01,199 --> 00:41:01,559
Fine.

795
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:03,480
Then I'll bet my life against yours.

796
00:41:15,840 --> 00:41:17,119
I've got three Kings.

797
00:41:19,559 --> 00:41:20,199
How can you beat me?

798
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:24,440
You little punk, your life

799
00:41:24,440 --> 00:41:25,320
belongs to me now.

800
00:41:32,159 --> 00:41:32,559
Five.

801
00:41:35,559 --> 00:41:35,960
Two.

802
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:40,320
Three.

803
00:41:42,280 --> 00:41:43,679
Beats three of a kind.

804
00:41:54,679 --> 00:41:55,159
What's wrong?

805
00:42:32,880 --> 00:42:33,840
You know Red Leaf well, right?

806
00:42:34,079 --> 00:42:34,440
I do.

807
00:42:37,519 --> 00:42:38,400
Help me find someone.

808
00:43:12,079 --> 00:43:13,719
The work of the Publicity Department

809
00:43:13,719 --> 00:43:16,199
needs someone to systematically take charge of it.

810
00:43:16,199 --> 00:43:17,599
We're getting ready to close the net.

811
00:43:17,599 --> 00:43:19,920
Word has spread all over the City Bureau

812
00:43:19,920 --> 00:43:21,320
that even carrying a camera,

813
00:43:21,320 --> 00:43:22,480
we can still catch drug dealers.

814
00:43:22,480 --> 00:43:23,440
How did you come up with the idea

815
00:43:23,440 --> 00:43:25,000
to make our Special Police Unit

816
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:26,840
the theme of this Police Open Day?

817
00:43:26,840 --> 00:43:27,760
We are Special Police,

818
00:43:27,760 --> 00:43:28,719
not actors.

819
00:43:28,719 --> 00:43:30,480
Everyone in the Special Police Unit is full of energy.

820
00:43:30,480 --> 00:43:31,480
You've trained them well.

821
00:43:31,480 --> 00:43:33,960
But many things can't be solved with brawn alone.

822
00:43:33,960 --> 00:43:35,760
Sometimes, you need to use your brain.
